# Play test of Shelter Atoll (CIPlay shelter_atoll, in a test world 'CI ...'). Points as in its recipe; the shelter's
# floor is 1.69 m above the sea, the roof slab 7.75 m.
island Shelter Atoll
# DEEP 10-25: the dune moved the land's centre (the recipe's save prints the exact offset)
offset 14.7199 -1.3105
expect step 0
expect title Shelter No. 7

# Over the land bridge from the ring onto the islet's roof slab: the hatch and its notice
walk 30 0 to 22 0 to 16 1 to 8 6 h=7.75
zone roof
expect step 0
read Shelter notice
expect step 1

# DEEP 10-25: Lookout Dune on the ring's west side, the lookout's log and her cache
zone dunefoot
zone dunetop
expect step 2
read Lookout Nadia Ferris's log
expect step 3
use dunehatch
expect message The hatch lifts

# ABYSS 10-26: Radar Hill's valve, the patrol boat's coil (a dive), the relay box north of the slab
zone radarfoot
zone radartop
expect step 4
open Radar deck box
expect story radarvalve 1
expect step 5
zone channel
expect step 6
read Dr. Ruth Calder's field note
air boatair
open Patrol boat locker
expect story sigcoil 1
expect step 7
use relaybox
expect story sheltrelay 1
expect step 8
expect shown relaychest
open Relay chest
read Relay crew's card

# ABYSS 10-26 secrets: the runway lights (2 and 4 start lit; 2, 3 and 4 light them all), the dog tags, the maze's
# heart, the supply plane, the ammo cave
zone barrier
expect hidden signallocker
use Runway light 2
use Runway light 3
use Runway light 4
wait 1
expect shown signallocker
open Signal locker
use Dog tag 1
use Dog tag 2
use Dog tag 3
use Dog tag 4
use Dog tag 5
wait 1
expect message All five dog tags
expect item TitaniumIngot 1
zone decongate
zone deconheart
open Decon crew's chest
open Supply plane's crate
zone ammocave
open Ammo cave's chest

# Down the hatch: through the collar to the hall's floor; the ladder takes hold at the top and at the foot
expect stand 0 5.6 h=1.69
climb 0 7.1 h=6.3
climb 0 7.1 h=0.3
at 0 4 h=1.9
zone hatchhall
expect step 9
expect message red light turns

# The main hall into the radio room: the radio log
walk 0 4 to 2 2 to 2 0 to 4 0 to 6.5 -0.8 h=1.69 below=5
read Radio log
expect step 10
use opradio
expect message radio is dead

# The generator room: the generator is dry; the commander's door and the blast gate stay shut
walk 6.5 -0.8 to 2 -0.5 to 1.8 -2 to 0 -5 to -3 -6 to -5.5 -6.5 h=1.69 below=5
use generator
expect message bone dry
expect hidden lamps
expect shown dark
walk -2 -6 to 4.5 -6 h=1.69 below=5 blocked
walk -2 -4.3 to 4.5 -4.3 h=1.69 below=5 blocked
walk -2 -7.7 to 4.5 -7.7 h=1.69 below=5 blocked
walk 0 -6 to 0 -12 h=1.69 below=5 blocked

# The dormitory: three big rats in the bunks, the radio operator's locker with the fuel
walk 0 -6 to -1.8 -2 to -2 0 to -5 0.5 h=1.69 below=5
zone dorm
expect message rats, big ones
kill Rat
expect step 11
expect animals Rat 0
open Bunk locker
expect story fuel 1
expect step 12

# The generator runs: lamps on, the dark air gone, the commander's door and the blast gate open
walk -5 0.5 to -2 0 to -1.8 -2 to 0 -5 to -3 -6 to -5.5 -6.5 h=1.69 below=5
use generator
expect message coughs, sputters
expect story fuel 0
expect shown lamps
expect hidden dark
expect shown hum
wait 7

# Through the commander's door: his orders and his safe
walk -5.5 -6.5 to -3 -6 to 0 -6 to 4 -6 to 4.2 -8.3 to 6.6 -8.2 h=1.69 below=5
read Commander's orders
expect step 13
open Commander's safe
wait 2
expect item Blueprint_Fueltank 1
expect done

# Out through the blast gate onto the landing
walk 6.6 -8.2 to 4.2 -8.3 to 4 -6 to 0 -6 to 0 -9.5 to 0 -12.5 h=1.68 below=5
expect stand 0 -12.5 h=1.68
zone outside
expect message Daylight

# The radio room's set runs on the generator now (Raft's radio: power or a battery)
use opradio
expect message Static crackles
